<title>UK: Glaxo sees stg cutting '97 profit, sales.</title>
<headline>Glaxo sees stg cutting '97 profit, sales.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>British drugs group Glaxo Wellcome Plc said on Thursday it expected full-year sales and profits to be reduced by around eight percent as a result of the strength of sterling.</p>
<p>In a telephone interview with Reuters, chairman and chief executive Sir Richard Sykes said this was an improvement from the reduction of 10 percent in first-half profits and sales caused by the pound's rise of around seven percent against the dollar and 20 percent against European currencies.</p>
</text>
